axes.model_access:
The official model-selector page states three usage tiers: Auto smart routing, Fast tier, direct model selection;
the selectable list includes the Qwen3.8/3.7 series, DeepSeek-V4-Pro/Flash, GLM-5.3/Flash, Kimi-K3/K2.8-Preview,
MiniMax-M3.1-Flash (each with a Credits usage reference factor; the list and factors follow the client);
you can also bring your own models via API keys (official "custom models" page; the CLI side calls it a BYOK wizard).
The series page's official line: "under the hood it supports GLM, DeepSeek, Kimi, MiniMax and other mainstream domestic LLMs".

axes.runtime:
Qoder CN is a product family (official family page): the all-in-one AI workspace Qoder CN (desktop app),
Qoder CN IDE, Qoder CN JetBrains plugin, Qoder CN CLI, Agent SDK (TypeScript/Python),
Cloud Agents CN (a fully managed cloud Agent platform), QoderWake CN (digital employees), mobile and web editions;
Credits are shared across products (subscription terms on the official account & subscription page). The coding mainline is the IDE/plugin/CLI trio;
the official "what is Qoder CN IDE" page states the VS Code plugin is no longer maintained.

axes.tools:
Official docs cover the full extension surface: MCP (connector marketplace or custom MCP servers, configured in ~/.qoder/settings.json),
Skills, Plugins, Subagents (expert teams: frontend/backend/database/ops/testing domain agents), Hooks, custom instructions and commands;
the CLI has built-in file read/write, Shell execution, Grep/Glob, web search and page fetching, with a non-interactive mode for scripts and CI/CD;
there is also Repo Wiki (generates project knowledge for a code repository) and code security scanning (progressive scans before commit/push).

axes.context:
The memory mechanism has official pages: two classes — global memory and project memory, each toggleable and clearable, stored in the local memory directory;
the official docs split context sources into three layers — memory (cross-task preferences and background), Repo Wiki (project knowledge generated from the codebase),
knowledge base (structured material maintained by teams); there is also context compaction, codebase indexing, rule settings, multimodal input (images/PDF).

axes.permissions:
Account system (Alibaba Cloud account); the CLI has permission modes, rule configuration and a tool-call approval flow (official permissions page);
the terminal & sandbox page states that running project commands during tasks and reviewing operations that need authorization requires approval;
the security & authorization page gives a checklist for accounts/credentials/extensions/connections. On the enterprise side there is an Enterprise Standard and an Enterprise Dedicated edition (VPC deployment).
